        {
            "_id": "MpLfJ77c5yG85ycd",
            "img": "systems/pf2e/icons/actions/Passive.webp",
            "name": "Sealskin Coat",
            "sort": 1000000,
            "system": {
                "actionType": {
                    "value": "passive"
                },
                "actions": {
                    "value": null
                },
                "category": "interaction",
                "description": {
                    "value": "<p>A selkie can slip their seal pelt on and off as a sealskin coat. They're permanently bound to it and can sense its location if separated (as the locate spell). While wearing their sealskin coat, the selkie is immune to mild, severe, and extreme cold, and treats incredible cold as severe cold. They can also speak with seals (as speak with animals). When the selkie uses Change Shape, they must draw their sealskin coat around themself to become a seal or fully remove it to become a human. They can't leave their human form if their sealskin coat isn't in their possession.</p>\n<p>If their sealskin coat is destroyed, the selkie feels its loss as an ever-present wound. They take a −1 status penalty to all attacks and saving throws, but they gain a +1 status bonus to seaborn yearning's DC and their edge of mourning deals @Damage[2d6[mental]] damage instead of 1d6.</p>"
                },
                "publication": {
                    "license": "OGL",
                    "remaster": false,
                    "title": ""
                },
                "rules": [
                    {
                        "key": "RollOption",
                        "label": "PF2E.NPCAbility.Selkie.SealskinCoat.RollOptionLabel",
                        "option": "sealskin-coat",
                        "toggleable": true
                    },
                    {
                        "key": "FlatModifier",
