            "privateNotes": "",
            "publicNotes": "<p>The haunting songs that sometimes accompany pods of seals are from selkies, fey who freely shift between human and seal forms. Their natural forms belong fully to neither world, sporting a mix of human and seal features.</p>\n<p>Selkies move through the water and on the shore with equal ease, and seaside communities often talk of them as though they were the tide itself. Despite these poetic associations, however, the life of a selkie exists far beyond the imagination of land-bound mortals. For selkies, losing either the land or the sea is to lose a part of themselves. They eagerly seek kinship with others who exist in multiple worlds and are often found as surprise guests at the celebrations of azarketis or merfolk.</p>",
